# Tendril of the Mycotyrant: "{5}{G}{G}: Put seven +1/+1 counters on target noncreature land you control. It becomes a 0/0 Fungus creature with haste.
# It's still a land." Bot1 casts the Tendril on turn 1 (two Moxen of five, one Forest), then on turn 3 plays a second Forest and activates the ability
# on it, paying with the Moxen, the first Forest and Black Lotus (seven of the eight mana). The new Forest is a 7/7 Fungus land creature with haste
# (it came this turn and still attacks, CR 702.10) and Bot2 goes to 13. The Tendril is not a land: it was not a legal target. The ability states no
# duration (the ruling), so on Bot2's turn the Forest is still that creature.

